-One hour?

528
00:16:19,540 --> 00:16:20,730
Crap, we're not even packed.

529
00:16:20,730 --> 00:16:23,320
-If you don't, you and your
 spaceship will be destroyed.

530
00:16:23,320 --> 00:16:25,330
-You and your
 daughter are doomed.

531
00:16:25,330 --> 00:16:28,280
-Only 59 minutes remain.

532
00:16:28,280 --> 00:16:31,250
Lasvon, train the guns
 on their spaceship.

533
00:16:34,080 --> 00:16:35,360
59 minutes.

534
00:16:35,360 --> 00:16:36,810
-A CBS News magazine.

535
00:16:36,810 --> 00:16:38,400
-Come on, Rocky, Winky.

536
00:16:38,400 --> 00:16:39,960
It's useless.

537
00:16:39,960 --> 00:16:43,130
We're wasting our
 precious minutes.

538
00:16:43,130 --> 00:16:46,610
-"The Honeymooners!"

539
00:16:46,610 --> 00:16:47,990
-Well, we had plenty
 of time to spare.

540
00:16:47,990 --> 00:16:51,740
We could have hit the
 gift shop or something.

541
00:16:51,740 --> 00:16:53,490
-Boy, oh, boy.

542
00:16:53,490 --> 00:16:55,170
-It's pretty slow for a rocket.

543
00:16:58,770 --> 00:17:00,490
-Ah, Cleolanta.

544
00:17:00,490 --> 00:17:02,390
A stubborn woman
 if I ever saw one.

545
00:17:02,390 --> 00:17:03,440
-You've never see one, Rocky.

546
00:17:03,440 --> 00:17:04,910
-You can't argue with
 self-sufficient people

547
00:17:04,910 --> 00:17:05,650
like that.

548
00:17:05,650 --> 00:17:07,790
-Well, now me, I--
 I'm a family guy.

549
00:17:07,790 --> 00:17:08,770
I like my neighbors.

550
00:17:08,770 --> 00:17:11,130
You know, how about
 a game of cards.

551
00:17:11,130 --> 00:17:12,760
Or may I borrow a cup of sugar?

552
00:17:12,760 --> 00:17:13,670
-Can I see your butt?

553
00:17:16,270 --> 00:17:18,240
-Orbit Jet to
 Space Station OW-9.

554
00:17:22,780 --> 00:17:23,280
[BEEPING]

555
00:17:23,280 --> 00:17:24,640
-Won't Rocky be surprised?

556
00:17:24,640 --> 00:17:27,580
-When I tell him I'm pregnant!

557
00:17:27,580 --> 00:17:30,460
Station OW-9 to Orbit Jet.

558
00:17:30,460 --> 00:17:31,940
Andrews to Rocky Jones.

559
00:17:31,940 --> 00:17:32,500
Come in, Rocky.

560
00:17:32,500 --> 00:17:33,000
-Hm?

561
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:35,080
I'm using my space voice.

562
00:17:35,080 --> 00:17:36,730
-OW-9 to Orbit Jet.

563
00:17:36,730 --> 00:17:38,460
Come in, Rocky Jones.

564
00:17:38,460 --> 00:17:39,860
-Well, what's the
 matter with Andrews?

565
00:17:39,860 --> 00:17:41,660
Has he got a mouth full
 of crackers, or something?

566
00:17:41,660 --> 00:17:44,020
-No, he's got an
 extra Y chromosome.

567
00:17:44,020 --> 00:17:45,910
-Rocket Jones to OW-9.

568
00:17:45,910 --> 00:17:47,880
Come in, OW-9.

569
00:17:47,880 --> 00:17:49,440
Andrews to Rocky Jones.

570
00:17:49,440 --> 00:17:50,090
Come in.

571
00:17:50,090 --> 00:17:51,070
-Heh, heh.

572
00:17:51,070 --> 00:17:53,510
[CHUCKLING]

573
00:17:53,510 --> 00:17:54,290
-Goodness, gracious!

574
00:17:54,290 --> 00:17:55,550
-Great balls of fire!

575
00:17:58,550 --> 00:18:01,860
-That's Professor Newton,
 and Vina and Bobby.

576
00:18:01,860 --> 00:18:02,860
-That's right, Winky.

577
00:18:02,860 --> 00:18:03,870
We're all here.

578
00:18:03,870 --> 00:18:05,020
-And this is "Your Life."

579
00:18:05,020 --> 00:18:07,540
-Say, what are you doing
 on Space Station OW-9?

580
00:18:07,540 --> 00:18:09,320
-Oh, we're having
 a Mary Kay party.

581
00:18:09,320 --> 00:18:12,660
-We're here to greet old
 friends, Rocky-- Potonda,

582
00:18:12,660 --> 00:18:15,150
Bavarro, and Torvak.

583
00:18:15,150 --> 00:18:15,650
-What?

584
00:18:15,650 --> 00:18:18,230
Did they manage to build
 a spaceship of their own?

585
00:18:18,230 --> 00:18:19,940
-Winky, honey, hang up the line.

586
00:18:19,940 --> 00:18:22,180
-The Gypsy Moons,
 Posita and Nagato,

587
00:18:22,180 --> 00:18:23,940
are entering our solar system.

588
00:18:23,940 --> 00:18:24,900
Placenta and Neg--

589
00:18:24,900 --> 00:18:30,760
-And at 0600 today, they will be
 very close this space station.

590
00:18:30,760 --> 00:18:32,310
-Not close enough to wave.

591
00:18:32,310 --> 00:18:34,600
But close enough to dock.

592
00:18:34,600 --> 00:18:35,380
-Professor Newton--

593
00:18:35,380 --> 00:18:36,740
-Please hit Bobby.

594
00:18:36,740 --> 00:18:40,140
-Where will the space station be
 in relation to the Gypsy Moons?

595
00:18:40,140 --> 00:18:42,760
-Directly between them, Rocky.

596
00:18:42,760 --> 00:18:43,470
-Andrews?

597
00:18:43,470 --> 00:18:43,970
-Hm?

598
00:18:43,970 --> 00:18:46,450
-Yes, Rocky, great
 news, isn't it?

599
00:18:46,450 --> 00:18:46,950
-Stand by.

600
00:18:46,950 --> 00:18:48,690
I'll check back as
 soon as possible.

601
00:18:48,690 --> 00:18:49,400
Out.

602
00:18:49,400 --> 00:18:50,830
Winky, stay at the controls.

603
00:18:50,830 --> 00:18:51,560
Correct direction.

604
00:18:51,560 --> 00:18:52,910
Head for Space Station OW-9.

605
00:18:52,910 --> 00:18:53,920
-I gotta go potty.

606
00:18:57,360 --> 00:18:59,050
-OK, let's see how
 we start this here.

607
00:18:59,050 --> 00:19:01,720
Uh-- Dear Abby, I'm
 an elderly woman

608
00:19:01,720 --> 00:19:03,810
who doesn't enjoy sex anymore.

609
00:19:03,810 --> 00:19:05,430
I found that in the--

610
00:19:05,430 --> 00:19:06,940
What is it, Rocky?

611
00:19:06,940 --> 00:19:10,080
-Something Professor Newton
 overlooked-- the atmosphere

612
00:19:10,080 --> 00:19:12,550
chain which links the two moons.

613
00:19:12,550 --> 00:19:15,470
Now assume this is
 the space station.

614
00:19:15,470 --> 00:19:17,030
-And this is the ship
 arriving too late

615
00:19:17,030 --> 00:19:17,920
to save a drowning witch.

616
00:19:17,920 --> 00:19:20,210
-And these are the Gypsy
 Moons, Posita and Nagato--

617
00:19:20,210 --> 00:19:20,710
-Hm.

618
00:19:20,710 --> 00:19:22,400
- --approaching
 from that direction.

619
00:19:22,400 --> 00:19:23,150
-Neat.

620
00:19:23,150 --> 00:19:24,490
-Now as the moons pass--

621
00:19:24,490 --> 00:19:24,990
-Mm, hm.

622
00:19:24,990 --> 00:19:27,460
- --the atmosphere chain will
 envelope the space station.

623
00:19:27,460 --> 00:19:28,150
-Oh!
 Neat.

624
00:19:28,150 --> 00:19:28,650
Funny.

625
00:19:28,650 --> 00:19:30,370
-It was built only
 to stand in space.

626
00:19:30,370 --> 00:19:30,870
-Cute.

627
00:19:30,870 --> 00:19:33,410
-A sudden whoosh of
 atmosphere could destroy it.

628
00:19:33,410 --> 00:19:33,910
-Wonderful.

629
00:19:33,910 --> 00:19:34,410
Mm, hm.

630
00:19:34,410 --> 00:19:35,840
-Where are we in
 relation to them?

631
00:19:35,840 --> 00:19:37,530
-This is out position, here.

632
00:19:37,530 --> 00:19:38,560
-Next to that TCBY.

633
00:19:38,560 --> 00:19:40,280
-I don't know whether we
 can reach Space Station

634
00:19:40,280 --> 00:19:43,390
OW-9 in time to evacuate it.

635
00:19:43,390 --> 00:19:44,420
-I'll try to make reservations.

636
00:19:49,270 --> 00:19:51,660
-I can't understand
 Rocky not being excited

637
00:19:51,660 --> 00:19:53,510
about the Gypsy Moons.

638
00:19:53,510 --> 00:19:56,230
-Maybe Mr. Secretary
 put the pressure on him.

639
00:19:56,230 --> 00:19:58,230
Perhaps he didn't like
 our blasting off Earth

640
00:19:58,230 --> 00:19:58,920
without orders.

641
00:19:58,920 --> 00:20:00,320
-Maybe he thinks
 he's too good for us.

642
00:20:00,320 --> 00:20:02,270
Well, screw, Rocky.

643
00:20:02,270 --> 00:20:04,280
-Well, I can't think
 of any other reason.

644
00:20:04,280 --> 00:20:06,820
[BEEPING]

645
00:20:06,820 --> 00:20:10,110
-Orbit Jet to
 Space Station OW-9.

646
00:20:10,110 --> 00:20:11,110
Rocky Jones to Andrews.

647
00:20:11,110 --> 00:20:12,320
Come in Andrews.

648
00:20:12,320 --> 00:20:12,820
-Yes, Rocky?

649
00:20:12,820 --> 00:20:13,320
-Whoa!

650
00:20:13,320 --> 00:20:14,970
Got enough Maybelline
 on there, Skipper?

651
00:20:14,970 --> 00:20:16,180
-Give me your
 refueling schedule.

652
00:20:16,180 --> 00:20:18,160
When's the next spaceship due?

653
00:20:18,160 --> 00:20:19,430
-I'm having a
 Monteclaire moment.

654
00:20:19,430 --> 00:20:20,300
-Nothing scheduled, Rocky.

655
00:20:20,300 --> 00:20:23,320
Since Transport TR-14
 left, we're all clear.

656
00:20:23,320 --> 00:20:24,410
-I'll sing off.

657
00:20:24,410 --> 00:20:25,760
Call back the TR-14.

658
00:20:25,760 --> 00:20:26,890
Bring it back.

659
00:20:26,890 --> 00:20:28,450
-And back-fill the
 story for the audience.

660
00:20:28,450 --> 00:20:29,730
They have no idea
 what's going on.

661
00:20:29,730 --> 00:20:30,330
-What is it Rocky?

662
00:20:30,330 --> 00:20:31,890
What's the matter?

663
00:20:31,890 --> 00:20:34,180
-I have to clear
 for Andrews' call.

664
00:20:34,180 --> 00:20:37,370
Just remind Professor Newton
 of the atmosphere chain.

665
00:20:37,370 --> 00:20:38,220
-And hurry, Andrews.

666
00:20:38,220 --> 00:20:39,270
Make the call.

667
00:20:39,270 --> 00:20:40,300
Bring back but the TR-14.

668
00:20:40,300 --> 00:20:41,590
-Bring back the Boston Rag!

669
00:20:41,590 --> 00:20:43,720
-The atmosphere
 chain, Professor?

670
00:20:43,720 --> 00:20:46,160
-The atmosphere chain.

671
00:20:46,160 --> 00:20:49,430
Now, what can Rocky have m--

672
00:20:49,430 --> 00:20:50,740
-Oh, I've soiled myself again.

673
00:20:50,740 --> 00:20:51,290
-Of course!

674
00:20:51,290 --> 00:20:52,040
Of course!

675
00:20:52,040 --> 00:20:52,540
Oh!

676
00:20:52,540 --> 00:20:53,730
-He's a queer duck!

677
00:20:53,730 --> 00:20:54,760
-How stupid of me.

678
00:20:54,760 --> 00:20:56,850
-What is it, Professor?

679
00:20:56,850 --> 00:20:57,440
-Yes, what?

680
00:20:57,440 --> 00:20:57,940
-What?

681
00:20:57,940 --> 00:21:01,250
-Quick Andrews, make
 your call, as Rocky said.

682
00:21:01,250 --> 00:21:04,260
Space Station OW-9
 to Transport TR-14.

683
00:21:04,260 --> 00:21:06,120
Come in, TR-14, come in.

684
00:21:06,120 --> 00:21:06,620
-Hm?

685
00:21:06,620 --> 00:21:07,650
Hm.

686
00:21:07,650 --> 00:21:09,090
-Vladimir Horowitz.

687
00:21:09,090 --> 00:21:10,510
-I've made a terrible blunder.

688
00:21:10,510 --> 00:21:11,040
I've--

689
00:21:11,040 --> 00:21:11,830
-I'll say.

690
00:21:11,830 --> 00:21:13,400
- --led you and Bobby
 into grave peril.

691
00:21:13,400 --> 00:21:15,060
-I don't care.

692
00:21:15,060 --> 00:21:15,560
-Aah!

693
00:21:15,560 --> 00:21:18,300
-The OW-9 is going
 to be destroyed!

694
00:21:18,300 --> 00:21:19,270
[GULP]

695
00:21:19,270 --> 00:21:21,530
-What do you mean, Professor?

696
00:21:21,530 --> 00:21:24,920
-An object built to withstand
 the elements of space

697
00:21:24,920 --> 00:21:27,500
cannot survive in an atmosphere!

698
00:21:27,500 --> 00:21:28,360
-Oh, like you know that!

699
00:21:28,360 --> 00:21:30,920
-The atmosphere
 chain, that's right!

700
00:21:30,920 --> 00:21:31,710
-Yep, I--

701
00:21:31,710 --> 00:21:34,310
-And Rocky wants the
 TR-14 to evacuate us.

702
00:21:34,310 --> 00:21:34,810
-Ugh!

703
00:21:34,810 --> 00:21:35,310
-Ick!

704
00:21:35,310 --> 00:21:40,550
-Space Station OW-9 to Transport
 TR-14, urgent, repeat urgent!

705
00:21:40,550 --> 00:21:42,670
Come in.

706
00:21:42,670 --> 00:21:43,810
I can't get an answer.

707
00:21:43,810 --> 00:21:45,590
Shall I call Rocky back?

708
00:21:45,590 --> 00:21:46,910
-He knows what's happening.

709
00:21:46,910 --> 00:21:48,520
He'll do everything possible.

710
00:21:48,520 --> 00:21:50,390
Keep trying the TR-14.

711
00:21:50,390 --> 00:21:51,650
-And keep reaching
 for the stars!

712
00:21:51,650 --> 00:21:54,370
-OW-9 to TR-14, come in.

713
00:21:54,370 --> 00:21:55,040
Mayday!

714
00:21:55,040 --> 00:21:57,010
Repeat, Mayday!

715
00:21:57,010 --> 00:22:01,600
Space Station OW-9 to
 Transport TR-14, mayday!

716
00:22:01,600 --> 00:22:02,140
Repeat, mayday!

717
00:22:02,140 --> 00:22:05,010
-Um, do you fellas have a
 chair I could on, or something?

718
00:22:05,010 --> 00:22:08,110
-I'm bleeding her now, Rocky,
 all the thrust she's got.

719
00:22:08,110 --> 00:22:08,940
-Jeez.

720
00:22:08,940 --> 00:22:12,690
-Space Station OW-9 to Transport
 TR-14, can you hear me?

721
00:22:12,690 --> 00:22:13,650
Turn back!

722
00:22:13,650 --> 00:22:16,070
Turn back!

723
00:22:16,070 --> 00:22:16,740
-I resent that!

724
00:22:16,740 --> 00:22:19,550
-Orbit Jet to
 Space Station OW-9.

725
00:22:19,550 --> 00:22:21,150
Rocky Jones to Andrews.

726
00:22:21,150 --> 00:22:22,630
-Yes, Rocky?

727
00:22:22,630 --> 00:22:23,980
-It's no use, Andrews.

728
00:22:23,980 --> 00:22:25,300
The TR-14 is beyond reach.

729
00:22:25,300 --> 00:22:27,090
-So deal with it, man.

730
00:22:27,090 --> 00:22:29,150
-Has Professor Newton
 rechecked his figures?

731
00:22:29,150 --> 00:22:29,650
-Hm?

732
00:22:29,650 --> 00:22:30,780
-Have you checked
 his credentials?

733
00:22:30,780 --> 00:22:32,010
-Yes, Rocky.

734
00:22:32,010 --> 00:22:33,290
And their absolute.

735
00:22:33,290 --> 00:22:33,790
- --ly.

736
00:22:33,790 --> 00:22:40,740
-The Gypsy Moons will pass the
 space station at 0600 today.

737
00:22:40,740 --> 00:22:43,570
-Don't worry, we'll get
 you off before then.

738
00:22:43,570 --> 00:22:44,360
-All right!

739
00:22:44,360 --> 00:22:46,410
Heh, heh.

740
00:22:46,410 --> 00:22:48,910
-Tell Andrews I'll call
 back every hour on the hour.

741
00:22:48,910 --> 00:22:51,670
-Then I start
 tossing out bodies.

742
00:22:51,670 --> 00:22:53,860
-Please, try to understand--

743
00:22:53,860 --> 00:22:54,550
-I'm a magic man.

744
00:22:54,550 --> 00:22:55,420
-(SINGING) A dun-dun, chh!

745
00:22:55,420 --> 00:22:57,780
A dun-dun hoo!

746
00:22:57,780 --> 00:23:00,300
- --but seeing out friends
 on the Gypsy Moons.

747
00:23:00,300 --> 00:23:01,710
-My entire life is a lie.

748
00:23:01,710 --> 00:23:03,910
-Oh, the Gypsy Moons.

749
00:23:03,910 --> 00:23:05,230
-The Gypsy Moons, huh?

750
00:23:05,230 --> 00:23:07,640
-Hey, that's a novel idea.

751
00:23:07,640 --> 00:23:08,490
-Have you a plan, Rocky?

752
00:23:08,490 --> 00:23:09,790
Something we can do?

753
00:23:09,790 --> 00:23:20,780
Leaving the space station
 before 0600 looks impossible.

754
00:23:20,780 --> 00:23:21,540
-Ha, ha.

755
00:23:21,540 --> 00:23:23,700
Oh, I hope you're
 enjoying today's film.

756
00:23:23,700 --> 00:23:26,750
And I certainly hope those
 Gypsy Moons don't crash.

757
00:23:26,750 --> 00:23:28,700
Did you know that the
 Gypsy Moons is actually

758
00:23:28,700 --> 00:23:31,810
a reference to a popular
 song title from the 1920s?

759
00:23:31,810 --> 00:23:32,820
Mm, hm.

760
00:23:32,820 --> 00:23:33,780
Don't remember?

761
00:23:33,780 --> 00:23:36,130
Well, here's our own
 Tom Servo, Gypsy,

762
00:23:36,130 --> 00:23:38,450
and Crow to help you out,
 doing their rendition

763
00:23:38,450 --> 00:23:39,560
of "The Gypsy Moons."

764
00:23:39,560 --> 00:23:40,780
Hit it kids.

765
00:23:40,780 --> 00:23:44,100
-Oh, I'm telling ya
 Gypsy, I love you.

766
00:23:44,100 --> 00:23:45,760
And I know I'd love you
 too, if only we could--

767
00:23:45,760 --> 00:23:48,230
-Why, you haven't a chance
 with a girl like her.

768
00:23:48,230 --> 00:23:49,900
It's me she cares for.

769
00:23:49,900 --> 00:23:51,170
Isn't that right, Gypsy?

770
00:23:51,170 --> 00:23:52,190
-I can't decide.

771
00:23:52,190 --> 00:23:53,610
Can't decide?

772
00:23:53,610 --> 00:23:54,690
Well, maybe this will help.

773
00:23:54,690 --> 00:23:55,720
[STRUMMING BANJO AND WHISTLING]

774
00:23:58,800 --> 00:23:59,980
-Ba-boom, ba-boom.

775
00:23:59,980 --> 00:24:03,230
-(SINGING) I can't
 sleep, or clean my room,

776
00:24:03,230 --> 00:24:07,610
[WHISTLING] since you and I
 first had our swoony swoon.

777
00:24:07,610 --> 00:24:08,320
-Ooh!

778
00:24:08,320 --> 00:24:12,790
-(SINGING) In early June under
 the clear blue Gypsy Moon.

779
00:24:12,790 --> 00:24:13,390
-Ooh, that's nice.

780
00:24:13,390 --> 00:24:14,280
-No, no, no.

781
00:24:14,280 --> 00:24:15,400
Don't listen to him, honey.

782
00:24:15,400 --> 00:24:16,110
Listen to me.

783
00:24:16,110 --> 00:24:16,610
-I should.

784
00:24:16,610 --> 00:24:18,390
(SINGING)- While
 others have their tune,

785
00:24:18,390 --> 00:24:20,530
I know that I was meant for you.

786
00:24:20,530 --> 00:24:21,030
-Ooh.

787
00:24:21,030 --> 00:24:22,650
-(SINGING) Yes one
 on one makes two,

788
00:24:22,650 --> 00:24:24,470
and that would be just
 me and you, honey!

789
00:24:24,470 --> 00:24:25,250
Wow!

790
00:24:25,250 --> 00:24:29,730
Strolling arm-in-arm under
 a Gyp-Gyp-Gypsy moon.

791
00:24:29,730 --> 00:24:30,990
-Oh, very good.

792
00:24:30,990 --> 00:24:31,980
-Take my hand.

793
