 more dangerous.

1053
00:33:17,420 --> 00:33:19,120
-Oh, I see what you
 mean, Professor Newton.

1054
00:33:19,120 --> 00:33:19,750
-Twisted old fruit.

1055
00:33:19,750 --> 00:33:22,340
-While the Gypsy Moons
 themselves aren't large,

1056
00:33:22,340 --> 00:33:24,010
the orbit they describe is.

1057
00:33:24,010 --> 00:33:26,150
-Like children of a playground.

1058
00:33:26,150 --> 00:33:27,090
-Uh, now, look, honey.

1059
00:33:27,090 --> 00:33:28,490
Why do you just go
 make some sandwiches?

1060
00:33:28,490 --> 00:33:28,990
OK?

1061
00:33:28,990 --> 00:33:29,910
-Here, let me show you.

1062
00:33:29,910 --> 00:33:31,240
Bobby.

1063
00:33:31,240 --> 00:33:32,340
The way they move
 through space--

1064
00:33:32,340 --> 00:33:33,170
-OK, hit it, Joe.

1065
00:33:33,170 --> 00:33:35,530
- --it's something like two
 children on a playground.

1066
00:33:35,530 --> 00:33:37,550
Bobby is Posita and
 I'm the other moon,

1067
00:33:37,550 --> 00:33:40,800
Nagato Our arms and hands
 are the atmosphere chain.

1068
00:33:40,800 --> 00:33:43,300
They move through space
 spinning around each other.

1069
00:33:43,300 --> 00:33:43,800
-Yeah, yeah.

1070
00:33:43,800 --> 00:33:45,690
And I guess the moons sing
 "Ring Around the Rosie!"

1071
00:33:45,690 --> 00:33:46,260
Get out!

1072
00:33:46,260 --> 00:33:47,720
Get out!

1073
00:33:47,720 --> 00:33:52,170
-But if I spin myself, I
 don't cover half as much area.

1074
00:33:52,170 --> 00:33:54,860
-So what would happen if one
 moon sat down and shut up?

1075
00:33:54,860 --> 00:33:55,500
-Now--

1076
00:33:55,500 --> 00:33:56,630
-Back to work.

1077
00:33:56,630 --> 00:33:58,370
- --this is my great
 concern, Rocky.

1078
00:33:58,370 --> 00:33:59,730
-Where are my gummy bears?

1079
00:33:59,730 --> 00:34:02,840
-Magnify this by tens
 of thousands of miles,

1080
00:34:02,840 --> 00:34:05,740
and you see-- you see
 what tremendous danger

1081
00:34:05,740 --> 00:34:06,710
we're confronted with.

1082
00:34:06,710 --> 00:34:08,510
-Uh, Vladimer, if you get
 to an issue that's relevant,

1083
00:34:08,510 --> 00:34:09,120
let us know.

1084
00:34:09,120 --> 00:34:11,410
-For example, say
 there's a planet

1085
00:34:11,410 --> 00:34:13,820
or a moon right over there.

1086
00:34:13,820 --> 00:34:14,480
-OK.

1087
00:34:14,480 --> 00:34:18,380
-Bobby, go ahead again.

1088
00:34:18,380 --> 00:34:19,350
-It's on my birthday!

1089
00:34:19,350 --> 00:34:20,490
-Mr. Secretary!

1090
00:34:20,490 --> 00:34:21,860
I'm sorry.

1091
00:34:21,860 --> 00:34:23,220
-What's going on?

1092
00:34:23,220 --> 00:34:24,470
-She blinded me with science!

1093
00:34:24,470 --> 00:34:26,840
-An illustration of an
 astronomical phenomenon,

1094
00:34:26,840 --> 00:34:28,080
Mr. Secretary.

1095
00:34:28,080 --> 00:34:31,980
-Yeah, it, uh, it seems
 that you are a planet, Mr.

1096
00:34:31,980 --> 00:34:34,230
Secretary, and Vena is Posita--

1097
00:34:34,230 --> 00:34:34,730
-Hm?

1098
00:34:34,730 --> 00:34:36,320
-And Bobby's Nagato.

1099
00:34:36,320 --> 00:34:37,050
-Hm?

1100
00:34:37,050 --> 00:34:38,270
-No, no, no.

1101
00:34:38,270 --> 00:34:40,960
Bobby is Posita
 and Vena is Nagato.

1102
00:34:40,960 --> 00:34:42,170
-In-A-Gadda-Da-Vida, baby!

1103
00:34:42,170 --> 00:34:44,670
-You-- you could really
 either be a planet or a moon,

1104
00:34:44,670 --> 00:34:46,460
but as it happens,
 you're planet.

1105
00:34:46,460 --> 00:34:49,390
So you see what happens?

1106
00:34:49,390 --> 00:34:49,950
-I uh--

1107
00:34:49,950 --> 00:34:52,060
-Bob Saget, ladies and
 gentlemen, Bob Saget.

1108
00:35:00,460 --> 00:35:02,820
-Orbit Jet to
 Posita headquarters.

1109
00:35:02,820 --> 00:35:04,000
-The baby's talking!

1110
00:35:04,000 --> 00:35:05,970
-Bavarro, come in, Bavarro.

1111
00:35:05,970 --> 00:35:07,060
-Infant one to mother!

1112
00:35:07,060 --> 00:35:08,500
-Come in, Bavarro.

1113
00:35:08,500 --> 00:35:09,000
-Bavarro!

1114
00:35:09,000 --> 00:35:11,810
Come Bavarro.

1115
00:35:11,810 --> 00:35:13,040
-What, Potonda?

1116
00:35:13,040 --> 00:35:14,920
We were going to speak
 they're language?

1117
00:35:14,920 --> 00:35:16,090
-(WITH GERMAN
 ACCENT) Say nothing.

1118
00:35:16,090 --> 00:35:17,850
-It is Squawky Jones.

1119
00:35:17,850 --> 00:35:18,950
-Squawky Jones?

1120
00:35:18,950 --> 00:35:20,400
-Now that's rude.

1121
00:35:20,400 --> 00:35:21,780
Come down Bavarro.

1122
00:35:21,780 --> 00:35:22,280
Talk to him.

1123
00:35:22,280 --> 00:35:24,490
-I married a Nazi.

1124
00:35:24,490 --> 00:35:26,570
-Orbit Jet to--

1125
00:35:26,570 --> 00:35:27,480
-Rocky Jones!

1126
00:35:27,480 --> 00:35:29,740
-My thumb is swollen and purple.

1127
00:35:29,740 --> 00:35:32,220
-We've tried to
 vex one language.

1128
00:35:32,220 --> 00:35:33,430
-My neighbor chatza.

1129
00:35:33,430 --> 00:35:34,850
-Ah, her hair changed sides.

1130
00:35:34,850 --> 00:35:35,830
Did you see that?

1131
00:35:35,830 --> 00:35:38,740
-Professor Newton, and--
 and Bobby, and Winky.

1132
00:35:38,740 --> 00:35:40,170
-And Poco and poopie
 pants, and greasy Dan.

1133
00:35:40,170 --> 00:35:43,690
-This is Dinky, uh, Winky--
 she's got me doing it.

1134
00:35:43,690 --> 00:35:46,680
Bobby and the Professor are
 with us, and so is Vena.

1135
00:35:46,680 --> 00:35:47,820
-Bavarro.

1136
00:35:47,820 --> 00:35:49,140
-Yes, Rocky.

1137
00:35:49,140 --> 00:35:50,810
-We're in the
 ellipse of your moon.

1138
00:35:50,810 --> 00:35:53,210
Landing time, 0214.

1139
00:35:53,210 --> 00:35:54,580
-Hurry in, Rocky.

1140
00:35:54,580 --> 00:35:56,410
This is so-- so clandindo.

1141
00:35:56,410 --> 00:35:58,330
Uh, clandindo--

1142
00:35:58,330 --> 00:35:58,980
-The sap!

1143
00:35:58,980 --> 00:36:01,990
Thinks he's on "Hogan's
 Heroes" already.

1144
00:36:01,990 --> 00:36:03,450
-Oop, I can't take a crap.

1145
00:36:03,450 --> 00:36:05,090
Bobby's my witness.

1146
00:36:05,090 --> 00:36:05,820
-He's right.

1147
00:36:08,420 --> 00:36:11,430
-Oh, they're landing on
 the planet of Magic Rocks.

1148
00:36:11,430 --> 00:36:11,930
-Ew.

1149
00:36:18,910 --> 00:36:22,680
-Welcome, to our cardboard home.

1150
00:36:22,680 --> 00:36:23,240
-By Vena!

1151
00:36:23,240 --> 00:36:25,320
Have fun at German camp!

1152
00:36:25,320 --> 00:36:27,390
-Contombo!

1153
00:36:27,390 --> 00:36:28,970
Contombo, Rocky!

1154
00:36:28,970 --> 00:36:29,750
-Is that Swahili?

1155
00:36:29,750 --> 00:36:32,190
-I have such wonderful
 news to share.

1156
00:36:32,190 --> 00:36:33,520
-Zorro painted mine house!

1157
00:36:33,520 --> 00:36:35,330
-You see how happy we--

1158
00:36:35,330 --> 00:36:36,860
-Horowitz is getting smaller.

1159
00:36:36,860 --> 00:36:37,360
-I know.

1160
00:36:37,360 --> 00:36:40,950
-I just couldn't bring
 myself to tell her.

1161
00:36:40,950 --> 00:36:43,350
-Can there be a
 mistake, Professor?

1162
00:36:43,350 --> 00:36:47,050
Is the collision between
 Ophecius and Posita inevitable?

1163
00:36:47,050 --> 00:36:49,680
-I double-checked
 my equations, Rocky.

1164
00:36:49,680 --> 00:36:51,690
-Yeah, ya double-checked
 'em last time, too.

1165
00:36:51,690 --> 00:36:54,120
- --the slightest
 margin for error.

1166
00:36:54,120 --> 00:36:56,230
-Ophecius, Cleolanta's
 planet, which

1167
00:36:56,230 --> 00:36:57,330
didn't need any
 help from anyone.

1168
00:36:57,330 --> 00:36:59,670
-Men, just ignore him.

1169
00:36:59,670 --> 00:37:01,770
-She'll need plenty, now.

1170
00:37:01,770 --> 00:37:03,360
A fleet of spaceships
 for evacuation.

1171
00:37:03,360 --> 00:37:04,370
-Shut up, Winky.

1172
00:37:04,370 --> 00:37:05,540
Just shut up!

1173
00:37:05,540 --> 00:37:08,060
-Bavarro, to him, his
 moon is a place of beauty.

1174
00:37:08,060 --> 00:37:10,330
His whole world.

1175
00:37:10,330 --> 00:37:10,830
-Sit down!

1176
00:37:10,830 --> 00:37:12,000
-Well, we'd better go.

1177
00:37:12,000 --> 00:37:14,950
He has to be told.

1178
00:37:14,950 --> 00:37:16,860
-Now he can be told!

1179
00:37:16,860 --> 00:37:18,080
-Uh, is someone gonna drive?

1180
00:37:18,080 --> 00:37:19,570
Uh, wait for me.

1181
00:37:19,570 --> 00:37:21,590
-Oh, Potonda, he's beautiful.

1182
00:37:21,590 --> 00:37:22,610
-I'll take him.

1183
00:37:22,610 --> 00:37:24,110
-Beautiful?

1184
00:37:24,110 --> 00:37:24,980
What is that, you say?

1185
00:37:24,980 --> 00:37:26,440
His mother is beautiful.

1186
00:37:26,440 --> 00:37:27,760
My son is strong.

1187
00:37:27,760 --> 00:37:28,530
[CHUCKLING]

1188
00:37:28,530 --> 00:37:29,940
-All right, then.

1189
00:37:29,940 --> 00:37:32,370
He's beautiful and strong.

1190
00:37:32,370 --> 00:37:33,230
-Good.

1191
00:37:33,230 --> 00:37:36,910
The next ruler of Posita, he
 will be beautiful and strong!

1192
00:37:36,910 --> 00:37:38,370
-Of za purest race!

1193
00:37:38,370 --> 00:37:39,450
[BELL SOUNDING]

1194
00:37:39,450 --> 00:37:40,840
-If you'd like to make a call.

1195
00:37:40,840 --> 00:37:41,340
-Wait here!

1196
00:37:41,340 --> 00:37:43,980
I wish to surprise
 Rocky with my son.

1197
00:37:43,980 --> 00:37:45,590
-He's gonna give Rocky his son?

1198
00:37:45,590 --> 00:37:47,310
[THUNDER]

1199
00:37:47,310 --> 00:37:49,190
-This gets him every time.

1200
00:37:49,190 --> 00:37:51,690
This is going to be a doozie!

1201
00:37:51,690 --> 00:37:52,490
-Rocky Jones!

1202
00:37:52,490 --> 00:37:53,480
-Hello, Bavarro.

1203
00:37:53,480 --> 00:37:55,790
-Welcome to Posita.

1204
00:37:55,790 --> 00:37:56,780
Bobby!

1205
00:37:56,780 --> 00:37:57,510
-Poopie?

1206
00:37:57,510 --> 00:37:59,150
-Why was I not
 lucky enough to have

1207
00:37:59,150 --> 00:38:02,350
a son who would grow up to
 be a fine boy like Bobby?

1208
00:38:02,350 --> 00:38:04,090
Welcome to Posita, Bobby.

1209
00:38:04,090 --> 00:38:04,590
-Ah, you smell.

1210
00:38:04,590 --> 00:38:05,440
-Welcome.

1211
00:38:05,440 --> 00:38:08,000
Then he could be a brave
 man, like Rocky Jones.

1212
00:38:08,000 --> 00:38:08,980
-Uh, who the hell are you?

1213
00:38:08,980 --> 00:38:10,920
-Oh, Bavarro, I want you
 to meet Secretary Drake.

1214
00:38:10,920 --> 00:38:11,470
-Bavarro.

1215
00:38:11,470 --> 00:38:14,970
-Or my son could be a great
 leader, like Secretary Drake.

1216
00:38:14,970 --> 00:38:16,720
I heard so much about
 you, Mr. Secretary.

1217
00:38:16,720 --> 00:38:17,320
Welcome to Posita.

1218
00:38:17,320 --> 00:38:18,610
-Man, they're dopple-gangers.

1219
00:38:18,610 --> 00:38:19,100
Look at 'em.

1220
00:38:19,100 --> 00:38:21,580
-Or my son could have
 a brilliant mind,

1221
00:38:21,580 --> 00:38:23,440
like Professor Newton, here.

1222
00:38:23,440 --> 00:38:24,640
Welcome, Professor.

1223
00:38:24,640 --> 00:38:26,210
-Bavarro, you honor me.

1224
00:38:26,210 --> 00:38:28,060
-Bavarro, and
 Bavano, and Bavarro.

1225
00:38:28,060 --> 00:38:29,110
Kliepsen.

1226
00:38:29,110 --> 00:38:29,940
-Hi, Bavarro.

1227
00:38:29,940 --> 00:38:30,810
-Oh, Hi, Winky.

1228
00:38:30,810 --> 00:38:31,310
-Winky!

1229
00:38:34,060 --> 00:38:36,670
Or like Winky, my
 son would, um--

1230
00:38:36,670 --> 00:38:38,810
-Would get beat up
 in the third grade.

1231
00:38:38,810 --> 00:38:42,010
-Would have a huge heart, and a
 wonderful twinkle in his eyes.

1232
00:38:42,010 --> 00:38:43,480
Gentlemen.

1233
00:38:43,480 --> 00:38:45,820
I was afraid we'll
 never meet again, Rocky.

1234
00:38:45,820 --> 00:38:48,430
My moon travels a
 lot, Mr. Secretary.

1235
00:38:48,430 --> 00:38:49,130
-Yes.

1236
00:38:49,130 --> 00:38:50,840
-You're a lonely
 man, aren't you?

1237
00:38:50,840 --> 00:38:52,290
-We've been targeting
 your course.

1238
00:38:52,290 --> 00:38:53,290
-Mel Torme!

1239
00:38:53,290 --> 00:38:57,480
-The way the Gypsy
 Moons, Posita and Nagato,

1240
00:38:57,480 --> 00:39:04,120
travel through space, it's
 an astronomical phenomenon!

1241
00:39:04,120 --> 00:39:05,150
-Pig Face!

1242
00:39:05,150 --> 00:39:06,340
-Ha, ha, ha.

1243
00:39:06,340 --> 00:39:08,260
What is phenom--

1244
00:39:08,260 --> 00:39:09,880
-Something unusual, Bavarro.

1245
00:39:09,880 --> 00:39:10,910
-Something that happens.

1246
00:39:10,910 --> 00:39:12,610
-You see the
 atmosphere which joins

1247
00:39:12,610 --> 00:39:14,640
the two moons serves as a chain.

1248
00:39:14,640 --> 00:39:15,820
-Uh-huh?

1249
00:39:15,820 --> 00:39:18,190
-One moon swings the
 other, then the other--

1250
00:39:18,190 --> 00:39:20,670
-And I swing both ways.

1251
00:39:20,670 --> 00:39:25,130
-Strange that we don't
 get, uh, uh, dizzy, huh?

1252
00:39:25,130 --> 00:39:27,140
-Bavarro, please,
 listen carefully.

1253
00:39:27,140 --> 00:39:28,010
-You're fired.

1254
00:39:28,010 --> 00:39:29,730
-On the 19th of next month--

1255
00:39:29,730 --> 00:39:30,340
-Where were you?

1256
00:39:30,340 --> 00:39:35,030
- --your moon, Posita
 will-- will crash,

1257
00:39:35,030 --> 00:39:36,360
head on, into Ophecius.

1258
00:39:36,360 --> 00:39:38,110
-Hm?

1259
00:39:38,110 --> 00:39:38,950
-Both will be destroyed.

1260
00:39:38,950 --> 00:39:39,990
-Just do London Bridges.

1261
00:39:39,990 --> 00:39:40,970
Show him how it works.

1262
00:39:40,970 --> 00:39:42,360
-What?

1263
00:39:42,360 --> 00:39:45,130
What are you saying?

1264
00:39:45,130 --> 00:39:46,810
Posita is going to be destroyed?

1265
00:39:46,810 --> 00:39:48,200
-Unless you buy
 these magazines, now.

1266
00:39:48,200 --> 00:39:50,290
-Yes, Bavarro.

1267
00:39:50,290 --> 00:39:51,260
-No.

1268
00:39:51,260 --> 00:39:52,710
-Oh, he's pleased to know it.

1269
00:39:52,710 --> 00:39:54,650
-It will not happen.

1270
00:39:54,650 --> 00:39:56,100
Never!

1271
00:39:56,100 --> 00:39:57,250
I will not let it happen!

1272
00:39:57,250 --> 00:39:57,750
Never!

1273
00:39:57,750 --> 00:39:58,750
-OK, we're convinced.

1274
00:39:58,750 --> 00:39:59,250
Fine!

1275
00:39:59,250 --> 00:40:02,310
-Now, now, little
 prince, don't cry.

1276
00:40:02,310 --> 00:40:03,140
-Oh, honey!

1277
00:40:03,140 --> 00:40:03,640
-Ooh!

1278
00:40:03,640 --> 00:40:05,570
[IMITATING POPEYE) Sweet Pea's
 trying to tell us somethun.

1279
00:40:07,800 --> 00:40:11,550
-You know, Vena, in
 some strange way,

1280
00:40:11,550 --> 00:40:15,040
our baby knew about Posita's
 tragedy before Rocky told us.

1281
00:40:15,040 --> 00:40:18,360
-Oh sure, everybody's
 baby is so smart.

1282
00:40:18,360 --> 00:40:21,810
-I have had great
 pride in Posita.

1283
00:40:21,810 --> 00:40:24,590
More than anything, I'm
 distressed that my son

1284
00:40:24,590 --> 00:40:26,930
shall lose his heritage.

1285
00:40:26,930 --> 00:40:27,430
-Coo-coo!

1286
00:40:27,430 --> 00:40:30,670
-How the people of
 Ophecius must hate us.

1287
00:40:30,670 --> 00:40:33,790
Their moon stands
 still in all innocence,

1288
00:40:33,790 --> 00:40:35,730
while we rush forward
 to destroy it.

1289
00:40:35,730 --> 00:40:38,020
-Got kind of a Spritz cookie
 cutter on his chest, there.

1290
00:40:38,020 --> 00:40:39,270
-Have they started
 the evacuation?

1291
00:40:39,270 --> 00:40:39,770
-Evac?

1292
00:40:39,770 --> 00:40:41,550
Oh, evacuation.

1293
00:40:41,550 --> 00:40:43,640
-They don't know
 what's going to happen.

1294
00:40:43,640 --> 00:40:47,160
-Ophecius is ruled by an
 arrogant woman named Cleolanta.

1295
00:40:47,160 --> 00:40:49,670
She won't allow her people
 any information about life

1296
00:40:49,670 --> 00:40:51,550
on other moons and planets.

1297
00:40:51,550 --> 00:40:53,300
-Even the possession
 of an astrophone set

1298
00:40:53,300 --> 00:40:55,270
is punishable by death.

1299
00:40:55,270 --> 00:40:57,050
We tried to reason
 with Cleolanta, but--

1300
00:40:57,050 --> 00:40:58,450
-And we secretly switched her--

1301
00:40:58,450 --> 00:41:01,110
-She even threatened to
 kill us, if we returned.

1302
00:41:01,110 --> 00:41:02,340
-But she must know.

1303
00:41:02,340 --> 00:41:03,700
She must be warned.

1304
00:41:03,700 --> 00:41:05,290
-She will be.

1305
00:41:05,290 --> 00:41:08,600
Mr. Secretary, may I suggest
 you go with Bavarro to Nagato,

1306
00:41:08,600 --> 00:41:10,920
and meet with Torvak, the ruler?

1307
00:41:10,920 --> 00:41:12,510
We'll need his help
 in the evacuation.

1308
00:41:12,510 --> 00:41:14,010
-Oh, yeah, I'll take
 orders from you.

1309
00:41:14,010 --> 00:41:15,010
-Professor Newton--

1310
00:41:15,010 --> 00:41:15,610
-You make cookies.

1311
00:41:15,610 --> 00:41:18,030
-You and Vena and Bobby will do
 what you can, here on Posita,

1312
00:41:18,030 --> 00:41:19,850
while Winky and I are gone.

1313
00:41:19,850 --> 00:41:22,100
There must not be any
 panic among the people.

1314
00:41:22,100 --> 00:41:23,690
-Yes, Rocky.

1315
00:41:23,690 --> 00:41:26,960
-Mr. Secretary, we'll leave
 for Ophecius immediately.

1316
00:41:26,960 --> 00:41:30,090
-Hey Rocky, couldn't we rig
 up a space anchor for Posita?

1317
00:41:30,090 --> 00:41:32,490
-No, we're not gonna
 rig up a space anchor!

1318
00:41:32,490 --> 00:41:33,890
-If we only could, Bobby.

1319
00:41:33,890 --> 00:41:35,140
That would be a great solution.

1320
00:41:37,710 --> 00:41:38,210
[THUNDER]

1321
00:41:38,210 --> 00:41:38,710
-Ha!

1322
00:41:38,710 --> 00:41:39,400
I love that pooper.

1323
00:41:44,960 --> 00:41:48,580
-When in the Ukraine,
 visit Chernobyl.

1324
00:41:48,580 --> 00:41:52,470
-So, um, who's leaving, here?

1325
00:41:52,470 --> 00:41:53,430
-Uh?

1326
00:41:53,430 --> 00:41:55,320
-Uh, we don't--

1327
00:41:55,320 --> 00:41:57,550
-Looks like the land of
 Dairy Queen gone wrong.

1328
00:42:02,070 --> 00:42:02,900
-But you can't marry Ken.

1329
00:42:02,900 --> 00:42:03,800
You don't love him.

1330
00:42:07,960 --> 00:42:10,490
-Trinka?

1331
00:42:10,490 --> 00:42:11,720
-Jump on.

1332
00:42:11,720 --> 00:42:13,390
-Well, aren't you proud of me?

1333
00:42:13,390 --> 00:42:15,980
Today, I have a special
 audience to Cleolanta.

1334
00:42:15,980 --> 00:42:18,630
My, uh, Suzerain says she has
 great plans in store for me.

1335
00:42:18,630 --> 00:42:20,990
-So why are you dressed
 as Liberace's chauffeur?

1336
00:42:20,990 --> 00:42:22,820
-Well, aren't you proud of me?

1337
00:42:22,820 --> 00:42:24,750
-We used to have
 plans, too, Atlasan.

1338
00:42:24,750 --> 00:42:25,250
-Hm.

1339
00:42:25,250 --> 00:42:28,040
-We were going to leave Ophecius
 and see how other people lived.

1340
00:42:28,040 --> 00:42:29,900
-To me, Ophecius comes first.

1341
00:42:29,900 --> 00:42:32,140
You're talking as foolishly
 as a child, Trinka.

1342
00:42:32,140 --> 00:42:33,390
-Yes, sir.

1343
00:42:33,390 --> 00:42:34,620
-And that's, uh, pretty foolish.

1344
00:42:34,620 --> 00:42:35,620
It's my point.

1345
00:42:38,470 --> 00:42:39,490
-Jeez!

1346
00:42:39,490 --> 00:42:42,840
And the women who love them!

1347
00:42:42,840 --> 00:42:46,820
-Glad she's dressed
 for her Rumplemintz ad.

1348
00:42:46,820 --> 00:42:49,180
-I better hit the bottle.

1349
00:42:49,180 --> 00:42:50,880
-Even in the future,
 booze satisfies.

1350
00:42:55,470 --> 00:42:55,970
-Hey!

1351
00:42:59,660 --> 00:43:01,020
-Breaker, breaker, good buddy.

1352
00:43:01,020 --> 00:43:03,940
This is the Hot Pagoda.

1353
00:43:03,940 --> 00:43:06,200
-Pigs in space!

1354
00:43:08,720 --> 00:43:12,450
-So, ya ever think you'd be just
 sitting here saying nothing?

1355
00:43:12,450 --> 00:43:14,150
-Well, there's Ophecius.

1356
00:43:14,150 --> 00:43:16,360
-This is your scalp
 before treatment, Winky.

1357
00:43:16,360 --> 00:43:17,550
-Cut rockets, Winky.

1358
00:43:17,550 --> 00:43:19,220
We'll stand off and try
 to get a message through.

1359
00:43:19,220 --> 00:43:22,390
-Uh, take a left here, and
 we'll try to parallel park.

1360
00:43:22,390 --> 00:43:24,720
-We'll be lucky if we can
 get through to Ophecius.

1361
00:43:24,720 --> 00:43:26,630
Cleolanta always jams
 and garbles our messages.

1362
00:43:26,630 --> 00:43:27,230
[GARBLED MUMBLING]

1363
00:43:27,230 --> 00:43:28,180
-You're right, Winky.

1364
00:43:28,180 --> 00:43:29,550
I know we can't get
 through to Cleolanta,

1365
00:43:29,550 --> 00:43:31,630
but we'll try for
 the underground.

1366
00:43:31,630 --> 00:43:33,440
You see, there's an
 underground faction there,

1367
00:43:33,440 --> 00:43:35,760
in favor of joining
 the United Worlds.

1368
00:43:35,760 --> 00:43:37,930
If they have a secret
 astrophone set,

1369
00:43:37,930 --> 00:43:39,620
they can relay my
 message to Cleolanta.

1370
00:43:39,620 --> 00:43:41,680
-You know, Rocky's got
 all of facial expressions

1371
00:43:41,680 --> 00:43:42,950
of Troy Tempest.

1372
00:43:42,950 --> 00:43:43,450
-This is--

1373
00:43:43,450 --> 00:43:43,950
-That's right.

1374
00:43:43,950 --> 00:43:45,560
- --Rocky Jones in the
 Space Ranger's ship,

1375
00:43:45,560 --> 00:43:48,420
Orbit Jet to Ophecius.

1376
00:43:48,420 --> 00:43:49,770
-Rocky Jones!

1377
00:43:49,770 --> 00:43:50,440
-Cybil Faulty.

1378
00:43:50,440 --> 00:43:52,020
-Alert Ophecius.

1379
00:43:52,020 --> 00:43:52,520
Alert.

1380
00:43:52,520 --> 00:43:53,260
Learn this.

1381
00:43:53,260 --> 00:43:54,340
-Ya, well, learn this, Rocky.

1382
00:43:54,340 --> 00:43:55,860
-The moons, Posita
 and Nagato are

1383
00:43:55,860 --> 00:43:58,200
traveling in our solar system.

1384
00:43:58,200 --> 00:43:59,040
On the 19th--

1385
00:43:59,040 --> 00:43:59,540
-Uh-huh.

1386
00:43:59,540 --> 00:44:00,410
- --the moon Posita will--

1387
00:44:00,410 --> 00:44:01,940
-(IMITATING STEWIE) Oh, I know.

1388
00:44:01,940 --> 00:44:02,760
I know!

1389
00:44:02,760 --> 00:44:05,590
-Cleolanta must be told at once!

1390
00:44:05,590 --> 00:44:08,490
An evacuation must be planned.

1391
00:44:08,490 --> 00:44:10,300
United World's offer
 all possible assistance.

1392
00:44:16,690 --> 00:44:19,370
-We all remember John
 Banner, Sergeant Schultz

1393
00:44:19,370 --> 00:44:21,540
from TVs "Hogan's
 Heroes," the sitcom

1394
00:44:21,540 --> 00:44:24,190
that pokes fun at wartime
 atrocities in such

1395
00:44:24,190 --> 00:44:25,850
a life-affirming way.

1396
00:44:25,850 --> 00:44:26,860
Yes, yes.

1397
00:44:26,860 --> 00:44:27,440
John Banner.

1398
00:44:27,440 --> 00:44:30,390
Probably the most affable man
 that ever walked this earth.

1399
00:44:30,390 --> 00:44:32,460
And now, with the
 Bannergram, you

1400
00:44:32,460 --> 00:44:35,000
can send John Banner
 and his warm greetings

1401
00:44:35,000 --> 00:44:37,900
anywhere-- across the
 street or across the nation.

1402
00:44:37,900 --> 00:44:40,820
-Yes John Banner, like
 Pope John the 23rd,

1403
00:44:40,820 --> 00:44:42,410
gathering little children
 unto his bosom, he--

1404
00:44:42,410 --> 00:44:44,420
-Oh, better than
 Pope John the 23rd.

1405
00:44:44,420 --> 00:44:45,300
-Uh, you're right.

1406
00:44:45,300 --> 00:44:46,010
Much better.

1407
00:44:46,010 --> 00:44:47,890
So cheer up Aunt Jean in Denver.

1408
00:44:47,890 --> 00:44:51,390
-Or congratulate Cousin Bob,
 for no reason at all, in Denver.

1409
00:44:51,390 --> 00:44:54,890
-Or just send John Banner
 to yourself, in Denver.

1410
00:44:54,890 --> 00:44:57,240
Believe me, you'll feel
 warm and wonderful.

1411
00:44:57,240 --> 00:44:58,940
Just pick up the phone and say--

1412
00:44:58,940 --> 00:45:00,260
-I want to send a Bannergram.

1413
00:45:00,260 --> 00:45:01,770
-A few quick keystrokes, and--

1414
00:45:01,770 --> 00:45:02,270
-Ha, ha, ha!

1415
00:45:02,270 --> 00:45:03,820
-John Banner for everyone!

1416
00:45:03,820 --> 00:45:05,210
Love and happiness.

1417
00:45:05,210 --> 00:45:07,340
-Hey, I, uh, Joel, I bet that's
 fun to send a Bannergram.

1418
00:45:07,340 --> 00:45:07,610
-Um, hm.

1419
00:45:07,610 --> 00:45:08,110
Go ahead.

1420
00:45:08,110 --> 00:45:08,640
-Uh, let me try.

1421
00:45:08,640 --> 00:45:09,140
Uh--

1422
00:45:09,140 --> 00:45:09,690
-Oh, no.

1423
00:45:09,690 --> 00:45:12,510
-Uh, I did it wrong, I
 sent a John Boehner-gram.

1424
00:45:12,510 --> 00:45:13,190
That's great.

1425
00:45:13,190 --> 00:45:14,460
-And I just sent a
 David Brenner-gram.

1426
00:45:14,460 --> 00:45:14,960
-Oh, no.

1427
00:45:14,960 --> 00:45:15,670
-Look out!

1428
00:45:15,670 --> 00:45:17,580
-Wait, I sent a
 Lucas Tanner-gram.

1429
00:45:17,580 --> 00:45:18,710
-A Lou Gosset Jr-gram.

1430
00:45:18,710 --> 00:45:19,630
Hoo-hoo.

1431
00:45:19,630 --> 00:45:20,820
-A Junior Samples-gram.

1432
00:45:20,820 --> 00:45:22,890
-A Whitman Sampler-gram.

1433
00:45:22,890 --> 00:45:23,510
Oh, no.

1434
00:45:23,510 --> 00:45:25,620
Now you've got me doing
 it, you little devils.

1435
00:45:25,620 --> 00:45:26,120
-Ah!

1436
00:45:26,120 --> 00:45:28,660
-But it's all a good example
 of the wholesome effect

1437
00:45:28,660 --> 00:45:32,090
John Banner brings to any
 family or social event.

1438
00:45:32,090 --> 00:45:35,700
Spontaneous fun, good-hearted
 enjoyment, likes you best.

1439
00:45:35,700 --> 00:45:37,280
-I love John Banner!

1440
00:45:37,280 --> 00:45:39,000
-Because he loves me.

1441
00:45:39,000 --> 00:45:39,640
-Hm.

1442
00:45:39,640 --> 00:45:40,520
-Here's one more.

1443
00:45:40,520 --> 00:45:43,680
-Oh no, you sent a
 David Mammogram, Crow!

1444
00:45:43,680 --> 00:45:44,530
-I know nothing!

1445
00:45:44,530 --> 00:45:45,220
Nothing!

1446
00:45:45,220 --> 00:45:45,720
-Look out!

1447
00:45:45,720 --> 00:45:46,600
We got movie-gram!

1448
00:45:58,470 --> 00:45:58,970
-Huh!

1449
00:45:58,970 --> 00:46:00,370
A wife, Blythe Danner-gram.

1450
00:46:00,370 --> 00:46:00,870
-Ha, ha, ha.

1451
00:46:00,870 --> 00:46:02,450
I think that's a great one.

1452
00:46:02,450 --> 00:46:03,230
-Well, that was a bust.

1453
00:46:03,230 --> 00:46:04,560
I was parading down
 the hall in my sash,

1454
00:46:04,560 --> 00:46:06,940
and the award ceremony doesn't
 even start till next week.

1455
00:46:06,940 --> 00:46:08,500
Trinka, will you forgive me?

1456
00:46:08,500 --> 00:46:09,670
-Of course, I will,
 Thunder Thighs.

1457
00:46:09,670 --> 00:46:12,030
-As you know, I-- I'm ambitious.

1458
00:46:12,030 --> 00:46:13,510
And I love Ophecius.

1459
00:46:13,510 --> 00:46:14,600
-And I'm not superstitious.

1460
00:46:14,600 --> 00:46:15,370
And you look delicious.

1461
00:46:15,370 --> 00:46:17,100
-I also love you, Trinka.

1462
00:46:17,100 --> 00:46:17,600
-Hey!

1463
00:46:17,600 --> 00:46:22,100
-Which is the greater
 love, uh, I don't know.

1464
00:46:22,100 --> 00:46:22,600
-Atlasan--

1465
00:46:22,600 --> 00:46:23,320
It's a paint-by-number
 Kandinsky,

1466
00:46:23,320 --> 00:46:24,180
up there on the wall.

1467
00:46:24,180 --> 00:46:25,970
-United Worlds offer
 all possible assistance.

1468
00:46:25,970 --> 00:46:26,860
-Huh?

1469
00:46:26,860 --> 00:46:27,760
-I'll repeat the message.

1470
00:46:27,760 --> 00:46:29,660
-You're wearing a wire,
 aren't ya, darling?

1471
00:46:29,660 --> 00:46:30,520
-United Worlds?

1472
00:46:30,520 --> 00:46:31,380
-I love that show.

1473
00:46:34,290 --> 00:46:35,590
-Trinka?

1474
00:46:35,590 --> 00:46:37,630
-Atlasan, please,
 please forgive me.

1475
00:46:37,630 --> 00:46:40,240
But you must listen to
 what the voice is saying.

1476
00:46:40,240 --> 00:46:41,960
-Hm?

1477
00:46:41,960 --> 00:46:44,190
-Now it's garbage!

1478
00:46:44,190 --> 00:46:46,820
-Uh-oh!

1479
00:46:46,820 --> 00:46:52,310
-This is Rocky Jones in the
 Orbit Jet, clear to Ophecius.

1480
00:46:52,310 --> 00:46:52,810
-Oh, boy.

1481
00:46:52,810 --> 00:46:54,930
-Well, I guess I'm
 not here, huh, Rocky?

1482
00:46:54,930 --> 00:46:57,530
-Think we got through, Rocky?

1483
00:46:57,530 --> 00:46:58,650
-I doubt it, Winky.

1484
00:46:58,650 --> 00:47:01,780
If Cleolanta heard our
 message, there'd be some reply.

1485
00:47:01,780 --> 00:47:04,800
A warning to stay clear,
 because she didn't believe us.

1486
00:47:04,800 --> 00:47:07,280
Or a demand that we
 prove our information.

1487
00:47:07,280 --> 00:47:07,990
-Hm.

1488
00:47:07,990 --> 00:47:08,920
-So?

1489
00:47:08,920 --> 00:47:10,090
-Oh, I don't know, Winky.

1490
00:47:10,090 --> 00:47:10,720
-Rockets on, Winky.

1491
00:47:10,720 --> 00:47:12,010
We'll attempt a landing.

1492
00:47:12,010 --> 00:47:13,010
-Aye, aye, sir.

1493
00:47:18,500 --> 00:47:19,880
-Huh.

1494
00:47:19,880 --> 00:47:21,640
-You know, it doesn't
 feel like a Thursday.

1495
00:47:21,640 --> 00:47:22,480
-Hm, mm.

1496
00:47:22,480 --> 00:47:24,810
Hm.

1497
00:47:24,810 --> 00:47:28,430
-My first lobotomy kit, by Sony.

1498
00:47:28,430 --> 00:47:31,920
-Who else is in this underground
 conspiracy against us?

1499
00:47:31,920 --> 00:47:33,200
-Oh, just Betty next door.

1500
00:47:33,200 --> 00:47:35,660
-I'm not in any conspiracy
 against Ophecius.

1501
00:47:35,660 --> 00:47:38,050
But you must listen to me.

1502
00:47:38,050 --> 00:47:39,020
-You'll answer my questions--

1503
00:47:39,020 --> 00:47:39,520
-Mm.

1504
00:47:39,520 --> 00:47:40,200
- --and that is all.

1505
00:47:40,200 --> 00:47:41,600
-Can I flick that thing
 off your forehead?

1506
00:47:41,600 --> 00:47:44,060
-Who else is in the conspiracy?

1507
00:47:44,060 --> 00:47:44,880
-No one.

1508
00:47:44,880 --> 00:47:46,880
I only wanted to hear
 how other people lived

1509
00:47:46,880 --> 00:47:48,310
and what they were like.

1510
00:47:48,310 --> 00:47:50,470
And I love Ophecius
 as much as you.

1511
00:47:50,470 --> 00:47:51,770
-You answer my
 Suzerain's questions,

1512
00:47:51,770 --> 00:47:53,200
and not one more word!

1513
00:47:53,200 --> 00:47:54,340
-That turns me on.

1514
00:47:54,340 --> 00:47:56,600
-That's very good, Atlasan.

1515
00:47:56,600 --> 00:47:58,100
Knowing the
 punishment, it wasn't

1516
00:47:58,100 --> 00:48:00,790
easy to report your
 wife's betrayal.

1517
00:48:00,790 --> 00:48:01,550
-Thank you, Cleolanta.

1518
00:48:01,550 --> 00:48:02,600
-I'm still mad at you, though.

1519
00:48:02,600 --> 00:48:04,880
-Cleolanta, my Suzerain.

1520
00:48:04,880 --> 00:48:05,380
-Yes?

1521
00:48:05,380 --> 00:48:06,310
-My Suzerain.

1522
00:48:06,310 --> 00:48:08,680
-There is a spaceship
 descending on Ophecius.

1523
00:48:08,680 --> 00:48:10,060
-It's Rocky Jones.

1524
00:48:10,060 --> 00:48:11,050
Please listen to him.

1525
00:48:11,050 --> 00:48:11,620
-Silence, Trinka.

1526
00:48:11,620 --> 00:48:13,940
My Suzerain does not need
 the advice of a traitor.

1527
00:48:16,880 --> 00:48:20,910
[IMITATING LONE
 RANGER THEME MUSIC]

1528
00:48:26,330 --> 00:48:28,340
-Atlasan, prepare to fire.

1529
00:48:28,340 --> 00:48:29,000
-You're fired.

1530
00:48:29,000 --> 00:48:29,500
Oh.

1531
00:48:35,300 --> 00:48:36,290
-Fire controls ready.

1532
00:48:36,290 --> 00:48:36,790
-No, Atlasan!

1533
00:48:39,520 --> 00:48:40,500
-Fire!

1534
00:48:40,500 --> 00:48:42,460
[ROCKET FIRED]

1535
00:48:42,460 --> 00:48:43,160
-Whoa!

1536
00:48:43,160 --> 00:48:45,860
Almost hit the string.

1537
00:48:45,860 --> 00:48:47,330
-That's heavy stuff
 they're throwing, Rocky.

1538
00:48:47,330 --> 00:48:48,380
-Who care.

1539
00:48:48,380 --> 00:48:49,150
Gee, we might die.

1540
00:48:49,150 --> 00:48:51,220
Oh, boy.

1541
00:48:51,220 --> 00:48:53,550
-The next one will do it.

1542
00:48:53,550 --> 00:48:54,960
Ready, Atlasan.

1543
00:48:54,960 --> 00:48:57,300
Ready and--

1544
00:48:57,300 --> 00:48:57,800
-Whoop!

1545
00:48:57,800 --> 00:48:58,600
-Please, Atlasan.

1546
00:48:58,600 --> 00:49:01,150
Don't start to fire again,
 or I shall have to kill you.

1547
00:49:01,150 --> 00:49:02,160
-"Thelma and Louise," 1999.

1548
00:49:02,160 --> 00:49:03,770
-Fire, Atlasan.

1549
00:49:03,770 --> 00:49:04,680
-Yes, my Suzerain.

1550
00:49:04,680 --> 00:49:05,870
-Then this will stop you.

1551
00:49:05,870 --> 00:49:06,820
-What a wingspan.

1552
00:49:06,820 --> 00:49:09,280
-Don't repeat the
 order, Cleolanta.

1553
00:49:09,280 --> 00:49:11,450
-She's got one look,
 and this is it.

1554
00:49:11,450 --> 00:49:11,950
-Hm.

1555
00:49:11,950 --> 00:49:14,840
-Friends are
 visiting from Europe.

1556
00:49:14,840 --> 00:49:17,070
-Watch out for the tricycle!

1557
00:49:17,070 --> 00:49:18,430
Oh!

1558
00:49:18,430 --> 00:49:20,240
Oh!

1559
00:49:20,240 --> 00:49:23,940
-You hit my tricycle!

1560
00:49:23,940 --> 00:49:27,210
-Lasvon, imprison that woman.

1561
00:49:27,210 --> 00:49:29,370
-Yes ma'am, live to serve ya!

1562
00:49:29,370 --> 00:49:31,560
-Atlasan!

1563
00:49:31,560 --> 00:49:35,110
-There's ham in the fridge,
 honey, and there's--

1564
00:49:35,110 --> 00:49:37,350
-15 years and just
 never know, do ya?

1565
00:49:37,350 --> 00:49:39,460
Hm!

1566
00:49:39,460 --> 00:49:41,510
-Not since "Fire
 Maidens of Outer Space"

1567
00:49:41,510 --> 00:49:44,320
has there been such a
 ladder scene so compelling.

1568
00:49:44,320 --> 00:49:45,690
[GROANING]

1569
00:49:48,630 --> 00:49:51,720
-Super City, you
 build it, by Marx.

1570
00:49:51,720 --> 00:49:52,630
-My hip broke.

1571
00:49:52,630 --> 00:49:54,610
-Hey, uh, Rocky,
 have ya ever had

1572
00:49:54,610 --> 00:49:56,720
a funny feeling you're
 about to get slugged?

1573
00:49:56,720 --> 00:49:57,920
-Here, let me
 complete the thought.

1574
00:49:57,920 --> 00:49:58,420
Boom!

1575
00:49:58,420 --> 00:50:01,660
-No matter what happens,
 Winky, don't fire.

1576
00:50:01,660 --> 00:50:02,400
-Hey, I'm new.

1577
00:50:02,400 --> 00:50:02,890
I'm Ralph.

1578
00:50:06,010 --> 00:50:08,250
-Oh, no! "Crash of
 the Moons" is on!

1579
00:50:08,250 --> 00:50:10,350
-Mm, mm, mm.

1580
00:50:10,350 --> 00:50:11,520
-Alert the guards.

1581
00:50:11,520 --> 00:50:13,720
-Uh, w-we are guards.

1582
00:50:13,720 --> 00:50:15,950
-I don't want them inside
 the city spreading lies

1583
00:50:15,950 --> 00:50:17,810
to my people about
 the United Worlds.

1584
00:50:20,910 --> 00:50:23,640
-She's wearing that arm band
 because her career is dead.

1585
00:50:23,640 --> 00:50:25,500
-Mm, hm.

1586
00:50:25,500 --> 00:50:27,320
-So that's when I
 got into stamps.

1587
00:50:27,320 --> 00:50:27,920
It's fun.

1588
00:50:30,760 --> 00:50:32,610
-Well, I don't see
 any welcome mat.

1589
00:50:32,610 --> 00:50:34,080
There isn't even a doorbell.

1590
00:50:34,080 --> 00:50:35,870
At least, when we were
 here with Secretary Drake,

1591
00:50:35,870 --> 00:50:36,930
they let us in.

1592
00:50:36,930 --> 00:50:40,090
-Winky, I want to
 hit you so hard.

1593
00:50:40,090 --> 00:50:40,780
-Hello!

1594
00:50:40,780 --> 00:50:43,300
It's important that
 we see Cleolanta.

1595
00:50:43,300 --> 00:50:45,270
-Who is it that wishes
 to see Cleolanta?

1596
00:50:45,270 --> 00:50:46,760
-Uh, we're selling candy.

1597
00:50:46,760 --> 00:50:50,050
Send boys like us to Jupiter.

1598
00:50:50,050 --> 00:50:52,750
-Oh, they've got, uh, no
 visible panty line, there.

1599
00:50:52,750 --> 00:50:55,760
-Climb every cheap set,
 till you find a plot.

1600
00:50:59,150 --> 00:51:01,220
-Come on, in or out
 you space pilots.

1601
00:51:01,220 --> 00:51:02,450
We're not trying to
 heat the outside.

1602
00:51:05,100 --> 00:51:06,430
-Ope, see, I told
 ya we shouldn't

1603
00:51:06,430 --> 00:51:09,680
have put those things there.

1604
00:51:09,680 --> 00:51:13,110
-(SINGING) Da-da da, da,
 da, da-da-da, da, duh.

1605
00:51:13,110 --> 00:51:14,090
Brrp, brrp.

1606
00:51:14,090 --> 00:51:15,570
-Hold it.

1607
00:51:15,570 --> 00:51:16,380
You all right, Winky?

1608
00:51:16,380 --> 00:51:16,990
-Sure, Skipper.

1609
00:51:16,990 --> 00:51:17,530
-All right.

1610
00:51:17,530 --> 00:51:19,130
Take us to Cleolanta.

1611
00:51:19,130 --> 00:51:19,790
Move!

1612
00:51:19,790 --> 00:51:20,600
-Take us to the river.

1613
00:51:20,600 --> 00:51:23,080
Drop us in the water.

1614
00:51:23,080 --> 00:51:25,100
-Huh, 2, 3, 4.

1615
00:51:25,100 --> 00:51:25,600
Huh--

1616
00:51:25,600 --> 00:51:27,410
--(SINGING CADENCE) We
 are in a crappy film.

1617
00:51:27,410 --> 00:51:29,320
-We are in a crappy film!

1618
00:51:29,320 --> 00:51:32,070
-Hup!

1619
00:51:32,070 --> 00:51:32,670
-All right, Winky.

1620
00:51:32,670 --> 00:51:34,750
-Drop 'em.

1621
00:51:34,750 --> 00:51:35,580
-Hm?

1622
00:51:35,580 --> 00:51:36,080
-Atlasan!

1623
00:51:36,080 --> 00:51:38,520
-Cleolanta, I don't-- I--
 I don't know what happened.

1624
00:51:38,520 --> 00:51:39,250
I was going down the--

1625
00:51:39,250 --> 00:51:42,210
-Cleolanta, you're going
 to sit down and listen

1626
00:51:42,210 --> 00:51:44,090
to every word I have to say.

1627
00:51:44,090 --> 00:51:45,910
-Sure, it's for your own good.

1628
00:51:45,910 --> 00:51:50,250
-You're going to sit down and
 think about what you've done.

1629
00:51:50,250 --> 00:51:51,720
-Next, on "Nick at Night."

1630
00:51:51,720 --> 00:51:52,790
-Come on, bring it in.

1631
00:51:52,790 --> 00:51:54,410
Come on, bring it--
 you're doing OK.

1632
00:51:54,410 --> 00:51:55,080
[BABY FUSSING]

1633
00:51:55,080 --> 00:51:55,780
[CLICKING TONGUE]

1634
00:51:55,780 --> 00:51:57,510
-Baby trapped in
 film eats own hand.

1635
00:51:57,510 --> 00:51:58,700
News at 11:00.

1636
00:51:58,700 --> 00:52:01,160
-And he's been so
 happy for days.

1637
00:52:01,160 --> 00:52:03,450
Laughing, and not
 a single whimper.

1638
00:52:03,450 --> 00:52:05,440
-Now he insists on eating.

1639
00:52:05,440 --> 00:52:06,830
-Yes, Mr. Secretary.

1640
00:52:06,830 --> 00:52:08,560
-This toaster speaks to me.

1641
00:52:08,560 --> 00:52:11,670
-Yes, I'll-- I'll
 tell her, at once.

1642
00:52:11,670 --> 00:52:14,440
Oh, and my very best regards--

1643
00:52:14,440 --> 00:52:15,790
-What a nut burger!

1644
00:52:15,790 --> 00:52:17,960
-And to Torvak.

1645
00:52:17,960 --> 00:52:19,310
Out.

1646
00:52:19,310 --> 00:52:21,400
-Alfred, to the bat cave.

1647
00:52:21,400 --> 00:52:23,120
-I just talked into
 the radio antenna.

1648
00:52:23,120 --> 00:52:24,160
Everything's fine.

1649
00:52:24,160 --> 00:52:25,380
[BABY CRYING]

1650
00:52:25,380 --> 00:52:26,100
-Vena--

1651
00:52:26,100 --> 00:52:26,700
-Shut that kid up!

1652
00:52:26,700 --> 00:52:29,020
-The meeting on Nagato has
 been successfully completed.

1653
00:52:29,020 --> 00:52:30,690
-Domo Arigato, Mr. Roboto.

1654
00:52:30,690 --> 00:52:34,000
-Torvak will gladly welcome the
 unfortunate people of Posita

1655
00:52:34,000 --> 00:52:34,490
to his moon.

1656
00:52:34,490 --> 00:52:35,430
[BABY CRYING]

1657
00:52:35,430 --> 00:52:37,570
-Oh, but, uh, when
 will Bavarro return?

1658
00:52:37,570 --> 00:52:38,210
-Coo-coo.
 Coo-coo.

1659
00:52:38,210 --> 00:52:38,930
Coo-coo.

1660
00:52:38,930 --> 00:52:41,510
-And I have concern for our son.

1661
00:52:41,510 --> 00:52:43,240
-He bit me, the
 little son of a--

1662
00:52:43,240 --> 00:52:47,030
-They are making plans for
 temporary housing on Nagato,

1663
00:52:47,030 --> 00:52:48,960
so we can start the evacuation.

1664
00:52:48,960 --> 00:52:50,400
-Ew!

1665
00:52:50,400 --> 00:52:51,710
-All right, we're
 going to go out there

1666
00:52:51,710 --> 00:52:53,710
and we're going to show this
 team what we've got, all right?

1667
00:52:53,710 --> 00:52:55,870
-No, Cleolanta, not
 a day must be wasted.

1668
00:52:55,870 --> 00:52:57,700
Not even a single hour.

1669
00:52:57,700 --> 00:52:58,920
-So lunch?

1670
00:52:58,920 --> 00:53:01,180
-Winky and I will return
 to Posita immediately

1671
00:53:01,180 --> 00:53:03,050
to help with their evacuation.

1672
00:53:03,050 --> 00:53:04,250
-But what about Ophecius?

1673
00:53:04,250 --> 00:53:05,520
(MOCKINGLY) What about Ophecius?

1674
00:53:05,520 --> 00:53:07,970
- --will be dispatched
 from the United Worlds.

1675
00:53:07,970 --> 00:53:10,240
They'll help you with your
 evacuation to a new world.

1676
00:53:10,240 --> 00:53:10,740
-Yuck.

1677
00:53:10,740 --> 00:53:13,200
-Which will be
 mutually agreed upon.

1678
00:53:13,200 --> 00:53:15,720
-They will tell me
 where to take my people?

1679
00:53:15,720 --> 00:53:16,380
-Hm!

1680
00:53:16,380 --> 00:53:17,340
-No, Cleolanta.

1681
00:53:17,340 --> 00:53:18,930
They'll only advise.

1682
00:53:18,930 --> 00:53:20,110
-For you!

1683
00:53:20,110 --> 00:53:22,010
-Please!

1684
00:53:22,010 --> 00:53:24,580
-Jeez, the Paris Peace
 Talks were easier than this.

1685
00:53:24,580 --> 00:53:27,100
-Let me speak, alone,
 with my lieutenants,

1686
00:53:27,100 --> 00:53:28,570
Atlasan and Lasvon.

1687
00:53:28,570 --> 00:53:30,080
-You can tell they're
 falling in love.

1688
00:53:30,080 --> 00:53:31,690
You can see the sparks.

1689
00:53:31,690 --> 00:53:32,340
-Mm, hm.

1690
00:53:32,340 --> 00:53:33,570
-All right, Cleolanta.

1691
00:53:33,570 --> 00:53:35,260
-I'm feeling stupid today.

1692
00:53:41,680 --> 00:53:42,460
-Cleolanta!

1693
00:53:42,460 --> 00:53:44,570
-I'm just going to put pre-heat.

1694
00:53:44,570 --> 00:53:46,110
-They must be silenced.

1695
00:53:46,110 --> 00:53:48,130
If word of the crash
 of moons leaked out,

1696
00:53:48,130 --> 00:53:49,750
there'd be panic
 here on Ophecius.

1697
00:53:49,750 --> 00:53:51,420
-We can't imagine why.

1698
00:53:51,420 --> 00:53:52,660
-Mm, mm.

1699
00:53:52,660 --> 00:53:57,140
-The gas will keep them inactive
 until I've decided what to do.

1700
00:53:57,140 --> 00:53:59,040
-[SNIFFING] Winky, you
 been eating cabbage?

1701
00:53:59,040 --> 00:54:00,650
-What is it?

1702
00:54:00,650 --> 00:54:04,440
-Quick, Winky, cover your face.

1703
00:54:04,440 --> 00:54:06,940
-No, no, more of your face!

1704
00:54:06,940 --> 00:54:08,870
-The vent, up there.

1705
00:54:08,870 --> 00:54:09,980
-No, that's the sconce.

1706
00:54:13,450 --> 00:54:15,030
-Come with me, Atlasan.

1707
00:54:15,030 --> 00:54:16,510
We will make our own plans.

1708
00:54:16,510 --> 00:54:17,010
-Heh, heh, heh.

1709
00:54:32,610 --> 00:54:33,110
-Hm?

1710
00:54:33,110 --> 00:54:37,060
-To be safe, Atlasan, we
 should explode Posita, here.

1711
00:54:37,060 --> 00:54:38,950
-If we exploded it
 there, Posita wouldn't

1712
00:54:38,950 --> 00:54:41,590
have a chance to
 evacuate all its people.

1713
00:54:41,590 --> 00:54:42,090
-Pshaw!

1714
00:54:42,090 --> 00:54:46,340
-This vagrant moon,
 Posita, aims to destroy us.

1715
00:54:46,340 --> 00:54:49,140
Instead, we will destroy it.

1716
00:54:49,140 --> 00:54:51,140
We act only for
 self-preservation.

1717
00:54:51,140 --> 00:54:52,320
-We're Republicans.

1718
00:54:52,320 --> 00:54:53,130
-Yes, my Suzerain.

1719
00:54:53,130 --> 00:54:54,670
-You're wearing
 the crown, honey.

1720
00:54:58,500 --> 00:54:59,000
-Hm?

1721
00:55:01,510 --> 00:55:02,730
-Oh, the cookies are done.

1722
00:55:02,730 --> 00:55:03,760
Tollhouse!

1723
00:55:03,760 --> 00:55:07,130
[SNORING]

1724
00:55:07,130 --> 00:55:08,600
-The trail, becomes her.

1725
00:55:08,600 --> 00:55:10,320
Hm, hm.

1726
00:55:10,320 --> 00:55:13,150
-It's the extermination
 room at the Fanta Suites.

1727
00:55:13,150 --> 00:55:14,600
-Hm?

1728
00:55:14,600 --> 00:55:15,720
Oon yellimon!

1729
00:55:15,720 --> 00:55:19,580
Oon yel-- uh, huh?

1730
00:55:19,580 --> 00:55:20,110
-Heh, heh, heh,.

1731
00:55:20,110 --> 00:55:21,700
This is my lucky day.

1732
00:55:26,230 --> 00:55:29,630
-So, um, are you still sore
 at me for turning you in?

1733
00:55:29,630 --> 00:55:31,230
Uh, hm?

1734
00:55:31,230 --> 00:55:32,020
Lamb chop!

1735
00:55:32,020 --> 00:55:33,530
Pumpkin!

1736
00:55:33,530 --> 00:55:34,460
Snooker!

1737
00:55:34,460 --> 00:55:35,780
-Trinka.

1738
00:55:35,780 --> 00:55:37,490
Trinka!

1739
00:55:37,490 --> 00:55:37,990
-Trinka.

1740
00:55:37,990 --> 00:55:39,560
Trinka, Trinka, doo!

1741
00:55:39,560 --> 00:55:42,730
-Atlasan, tell me we're home.

1742
00:55:42,730 --> 00:55:44,210
I had such a bad dream.

1743
00:55:44,210 --> 00:55:46,730
I want to hear you
 laugh and say, wake up.

1744
00:55:46,730 --> 00:55:47,620
Forget your dreams.

1745
00:55:47,620 --> 00:55:49,110
-Yeah, forget your dreams.

1746
00:55:49,110 --> 00:55:52,120
You're in prison, honey.

1747
00:55:52,120 --> 00:55:54,300
-But, Trinka, I did only what I
 thought was right for Ophecius.

1748
00:55:54,300 --> 00:55:54,800
-Oh.

1749
00:55:54,800 --> 00:55:56,880
-Did you kill Rocky Jones?

1750
00:55:56,880 --> 00:55:57,380
-No.

1751
00:55:57,380 --> 00:55:59,340
No, he's only asleep.

1752
00:55:59,340 --> 00:56:01,490
-Atlasan, did he get
 a chance to speak?

1753
00:56:01,490 --> 00:56:02,910
-Yes, Trinka.

1754
00:56:02,910 --> 00:56:06,440
And now I'll be a great man
 in the history of Ophecius.

1755
00:56:06,440 --> 00:56:07,790
The savior of our planet.

1756
00:56:07,790 --> 00:56:09,110
-Hm, hm.

1757
00:56:09,110 --> 00:56:09,610
-How?

1758
00:56:09,610 --> 00:56:10,990
-Uh, I-- I don't know.

1759
00:56:10,990 --> 00:56:12,140
- --on a spaceship.

1760
00:56:12,140 --> 00:56:15,790
We leave soon to intercept
 it's menacing moon.

1761
00:56:15,790 --> 00:56:17,860
It will be my honor to
 fire tritanic missiles

1762
00:56:17,860 --> 00:56:20,830
into Posita, which
 was save Ophecius.

1763
00:56:20,830 --> 00:56:22,060
-I love it when
 you talk that way.

1764
00:56:22,060 --> 00:56:23,790
-I'll give the order, Trinka.

1765
00:56:23,790 --> 00:56:25,900
And all I ask for
 is a full pardon.

1766
00:56:25,900 --> 00:56:27,020
-Do I have to quit my job?

1767
00:56:27,020 --> 00:56:27,970
-They're looking for you.

1768
00:56:27,970 --> 00:56:29,710
-But on the
 astrophone, Rocky Jones

1769
00:56:29,710 --> 00:56:31,540
said there are
 people on this moon.

1770
00:56:31,540 --> 00:56:32,820
-Trinka, that can't be helped.

1771
00:56:32,820 --> 00:56:33,620
-Atlasan.

1772
00:56:33,620 --> 00:56:34,120
-Hm?

1773
00:56:34,120 --> 00:56:35,590
-Report to landing base.

1774
00:56:35,590 --> 00:56:36,160
-Goodbye, Trinka.

1775
00:56:36,160 --> 00:56:37,490
-Boy, her voice carries.

1776
00:56:37,490 --> 00:56:38,670
-Wait.

1777
00:56:38,670 --> 00:56:40,080
Warn those people on Posita.

1778
00:56:40,080 --> 00:56:41,310
Give them a chance to live.

1779
00:56:41,310 --> 00:56:43,900
-Trinka, I'm only obeying
 Cleolanta's orders.

1780
00:56:43,900 --> 00:56:45,390
-I vas in Austria during da var!

1781
00:56:45,390 --> 00:56:47,260
-- --his life to warn us.

1782
00:56:47,260 --> 00:56:49,270
-Well, why don't you
 marry Rocky Jones then?

1783
00:56:49,270 --> 00:56:51,160
-We must do the same for others.

1784
00:56:51,160 --> 00:56:53,020
-Atlasan, report
 to landing base!

1785
00:56:53,020 --> 00:56:54,950
-I'm coming, you great cow!

1786
00:56:54,950 --> 00:56:57,950
0 go back to sleep, and
 know nothing until I return.

1787
00:56:57,950 --> 00:56:59,500
-Sorry about your
 death sentence, hun.

1788
00:56:59,500 --> 00:57:01,400
Bye bye.

1789
00:57:01,400 --> 00:57:03,700
-Uh, hun, would you
 turn on the gas again?

1790
00:57:03,700 --> 00:57:04,630
I'm tired.

1791
00:57:04,630 --> 00:57:06,390
Thanks a lot.

1792
00:57:06,390 --> 00:57:09,210
-One more look!

1793
00:57:09,210 --> 00:57:11,170
-Hey, she's flipping me off!

1794
00:57:11,170 --> 00:57:11,670
Huh!

1795
00:57:11,670 --> 00:57:12,170
That gal.

1796
00:57:16,620 --> 00:57:20,010
-Whoa, did I get really
 betrayed last night, or what?

1797
00:57:25,060 --> 00:57:25,700
-Oh, hi.

1798
00:57:25,700 --> 00:57:27,510
I was just coming to
 fluff your pillow.

1799
00:57:27,510 --> 00:57:29,670
-Trinka, you're a
 great deal wiser

1800
00:57:29,670 --> 00:57:32,170
than I am, and much favored.

1801
00:57:32,170 --> 00:57:34,890
You do whatever you think is
 best, but please be careful.

1802
00:57:34,890 --> 00:57:37,760
Lasvon is on guard, and
 he thinks you're asleep.

1803
00:57:37,760 --> 00:57:38,720
[APPROACHING FOOTSTEPS]

1804
00:57:38,720 --> 00:57:39,690
-Get in!

1805
00:57:39,690 --> 00:57:41,850
-Oh, I'm never going
 to get to kiss her!

1806
00:57:44,640 --> 00:57:45,970
-All right, a hundred
 bucks to whoever

1807
00:57:45,970 --> 00:57:47,180
can guess who's in that rocket.

1808
00:57:47,180 --> 00:57:47,680
-Really?

1809
00:57:47,680 --> 00:57:49,490
-Uh.

1810
00:57:49,490 --> 00:57:53,330
-Neither will I.

1811
00:57:53,330 --> 00:57:57,950
--(SINGING) As long
 as he needs-- huh?

1812
00:57:57,950 --> 00:57:58,450
Hm.

1813
00:58:04,850 --> 00:58:07,330
-Uh, look out, here
 comes Craig T Nelson.

1814
00:58:07,330 --> 00:58:08,900
--(SINGING) Becuase
 I'm bad, I'm bad.

1815
00:58:08,900 --> 00:58:10,520
Jo mo, doo-doo doo-doo.

1816
00:58:10,520 --> 00:58:11,390
-Jo mo?

1817
00:58:11,390 --> 00:58:12,840
-It's all right in there?

1818
00:58:12,840 --> 00:58:13,480
-All. right.

1819
00:58:17,480 --> 00:58:17,980
-Hm.

1820
00:58:17,980 --> 00:58:19,430
Well, I'm really stupid.

1821
